e Kohombana junction of Ampara - Mahaoya main road, approximately 23\u00a0km (14\u00a0mi) away from the Ampara town. The monastery has been formally recognised by the Government as an archaeological site in Sri Lanka.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Samangala Aranya Senasanaya</b> or <b>Samangala Forest Hermitage</b> is an ancient Cave temple in Ampara, Sri Lanka. The temple is located west from the Kohombana junction of Ampara - Mahaoya main road, approximately 23\u00a0km (14\u00a0mi) away from the Ampara town. The monastery has been formally recognised by the Government as an archaeological site in Sri Lanka.</p>"}